{
 "type": "FeatureCollection",
 "metadata": {
  "note": "The Big Sandy and Cumberland Railroad (Virginia, inc. 25 Jan 1900) was a W. M. Ritter Lumber Co. 3 ft 6 in narrow-gauge logging road and common carrier running from Devon, W.Va. up Knox Creek to Hurley and Blackey, Va. (1905), then over the mountain to Rife (by 1911) and Grundy (late 1916). Mixed trains only. The N&W bought its stock on 12 Oct 1923, but the BS&C kept running its own trains. A standard-gauge rebuild and relocation was authorized in 1928 and opened 1928-31, and the N&W took over operation on 1 July 1931. The rebuilt line became the N&W Buchanan Branch. Three features: two BS&C features on the old narrow-gauge alignment, and the N&W Buchanan Branch on its 1931 alignment in N&W colour (the Rule 4 split is at 1 July 1931). No drawn years overlap.",
  "source": "research/branches/big_sandy_and_cumberland_railroad.txt (researched 2026-10-27): Virginia SCC annual reports FY1905, FY1906, FY1910, FY1913, 1919; 17 I.C.C. 569; Fowler's Virginia railroads list (branchline.uk); Railway Age 1931-32; Official Guide Feb 1952 Table 25; NWHS.",
  "pulled": "20261027",
  "freight_only_check": "No line here appears in a primary 'Freight Service only' table. These are omitted for lack of ANY passenger evidence, not because a source shows them freight-only: the Knox Creek Railway (1.4 mi leased link; folded into Devon - Blackey); Ritter's Levisa Fork extension Grundy - Ky. line; the N&W Levisa Branch and its 1944 extension; the 1936 Buchanan Branch Extension / Dismal Creek Branch; Ritter logging spurs; and the 1931-1947 years of the N&W Buchanan Branch.",
  "horsecar_check": "None: steam (geared Shay/Climax) throughout.",
  "ownership_split": "12 Oct 1923 N&W stock purchase is NOT a split (BS&C remained the operating company; it obtained the 1928 ICC rebuild order itself). 1 July 1931 N&W assumption of operation IS the split: BS&C features end at or before 1931, the N&W feature begins after it. Because the new line relocated most of the old one, the split is also a change of alignment.",
  "not_yet_sourced": [
   "BS&C Rife - Grundy (narrow gauge, opened late 1916): NOT DRAWN. The only evidence is BS&C system-wide passenger revenue for 1919. No timetable or station-level source puts a passenger train into Grundy on the narrow gauge (Fowler leaves Grundy unlettered). Wanted: a 1917-1930 Official Guide or BS&C timetable naming Grundy.",
   "BS&C passenger END: the Devon - Blackey and Blackey - Rife ends are [OPEN] at 1919. Nothing was found for 1920-1931. Wanted: Virginia SCC reports 1920-1930 (Table 8), ICC Statistics of Railways for Class II/III roads, a 1920s Official Guide, or the BS&C records (1900-32) in the Norfolk Southern collection at Virginia Tech.",
   "BS&C passenger START before FY1905 (construction began 1900; opening dates of 1901 and 1903 are claimed in secondary sources). Devon - Blackey's 1905 start is [OPEN].",
   "N&W Buchanan Branch first and last passenger years: drawn 1948-1951, both [OPEN]. Service may have begun any time from 1931 and ended after Nov 1951. Wanted: Warden & Miller, Norfolk and Western Passenger Service 1946-1971; N&W public timetables 1931-1960.",
   "Source conflict: the Big Sandy News (Catlettsburg, Ky.), 15 Oct 1909, says the BS&C had 'only been used for hauling lumber' and that passenger service would come with the extension past Blackey. This is against the sworn SCC passenger revenue for 1905 and 1906 and the 1908 figures in 17 I.C.C. 569. The primary figures are followed. The newspaper may mean a dedicated passenger train as opposed to mixed trains. Unresolved.",
   "Old-line mileage conflict: about 33 mi Devon - Grundy (carrier, ICC, N&W 1923, Hilton) against '44 miles' (Railway Age 14 Mar 1931). Not resolved.",
   "Exact narrow-gauge alignment Devon - Lower Elk (drawn along KY 2059), and where it crossed the Tug Fork at Devon. Also where the 1928-31 rebuild between Lower Elk and Hurley departs from the narrow-gauge trackbed.",
   "Location of Rife (Riffe): pinned beside Rife Cemetery (GNIS 1473216) on the BS&C grade; not confirmed by an era map.",
   "headway_min on both BS&C features and avg_speed_kmh on both BS&C features are estimates."
  ]
 },
 "features": [
