  {
   "type": "Feature",
   "properties": {
    "company": "Big Sandy and Cumberland Railroad",
    "line": "Big Sandy and Cumberland: Blackey – Rife",
    "id": "bsc-blackey-rife",
    "color": "#5C1A14",
    "mode": "intercity_rail",
    "avg_speed_kmh": 14,
    "speed_source": "Estimate only: narrow-gauge mixed train with geared engines over the mountain between Knox Creek and Slate Creek. No running times found.",
    "geometry_source": "OpenStreetMap via Overpass (maps.mail.ru mirror), routed with opstrace.py 2026-10-27; OSM way 168899678 (railway=abandoned, note:old_railway_operator=BS&C).",
    "geometry_quality": "7.9 mi drawn against ~9.8 mi documented (SCC: Devon - Blackey 17.30 mi in FY1910, Devon - Riffe 26.80 mi in FY1913, i.e. 9.5 mi). Fowler's mileposts give about 8 mi (Blackey MP 18, Matney MP 24, Rife MP 26). No straight-line legs. Traced end to end on OSM way 168899678, the 1931-abandoned 'Matney segment' grade over the mountain: Blackey - Wolford (Knox Creek) - summit - Matney - up Slate Creek to Rife. Its OSM fixme calls it a 'rough alignment', which probably explains why it runs about 20% short of the SCC figure. Rife (Riffe) has no OSM place node, and Nominatim returns wrong places (Waynesboro, Va.; Monroe Co., W.Va.). It is hand-pinned on the grade beside Rife Cemetery (GNIS 1473216), 1.9 mi up Slate Creek from Matney, which agrees with Fowler's Matney MP 24 - Rife MP 26. This is the line's only alignment. It is NOT the N&W Hurley - Raitt tunnel - Home Creek route, which replaced it in 1931. The grade continues east past Rife in OSM; that part is not drawn. A 0.6 km hairpin in the OSM way near the summit (37.333 N, 81.972 W), which runs out and back to within 90 m of itself, is cut at its neck; it may be a real horseshoe up a side hollow, but no era map was checked.",
    "segments": [
     {
      "start": 1911,
      "end": 1919,
      "headway_min": 1100,
      "note": "Mixed trains extended from Blackey over the mountain via Wolford, Rockhouse and Matney to Rife (Riffe), Va. 1911 is the first CONFIRMED year: Fowler letters Blackey, Wolford, Rockhouse and Matney 'a' (= 1911 BS&C public timetable) and Rife 'a(tm)', i.e. the 1911 terminus of service. The extension opened between mid-1910 (FY1910 still reported only to Blackey) and 1911. 1919 is the last CONFIRMED year, NOT a known end. It rests on the SCC's 1919 system-wide BS&C passenger revenue. Nothing has been found for 1920-1931, and the ICC let this segment be abandoned in 1931. Do not extend without evidence. headway_min 1100 is an ESTIMATE carried over from the FY1905 Devon - Blackey train-mile figure (~1.3 mixed round trips a day). No timetable frequency has been found for the extension.",
      "sources": [
       "Segment-level: start 1911 from Fowler's Virginia list, line 81 (legend 'a: 1911(BSC)t'; Rife lettered 'a(tm)' = terminus of service). Opening bracketed by SCC FY1910 (to Blackey, 17.30 mi) and FY1913 (to Riffe, 26.80 mi). End 1919 from the SCC calendar-1919 report (system-level passenger revenue only, no station-level evidence). 1931 abandonment from Railway Age 13 June 1931. Headway is an estimate.",
       "https://www.branchline.uk/jfpdf/virginiarrs.pdf",
       "https://archive.org/details/annualreportsta35commgoog",
       "https://archive.org/details/annualreportsta33commgoog",
       "https://archive.org/details/annualreportsta28commgoog",
       "https://archive.org/details/sim_railway-age_1931-06-13_90_24"
      ]
     }
    ]
