  {
   "type": "Feature",
   "properties": {
    "company": "Norfolk and Western Railway",
    "line": "Norfolk and Western: Buchanan Branch",
    "id": "nw-buchanan-branch",
    "color": "#023047",
    "mode": "intercity_rail",
    "avg_speed_kmh": 21,
    "speed_source": "Measured from the Official Guide card of 18 Nov 1951 (Feb 1952 issue, N&W Table 25): mixed M312 Devon 8:40 AM - Grundy 11:25 AM, 36.2 mi in 2 h 45 min = 21 km/h. Times were read from the page image.",
    "geometry_source": "OpenStreetMap via Overpass (maps.mail.ru mirror), routed with opstrace.py 2026-10-27; NS Buchanan Branch ways (old_railway_operator=N&W) plus the N&W main line (Williamson District) from Devon to the branch junction.",
    "geometry_quality": "35.8 mi drawn against 36.2 mi documented (Official Guide Table 25, Devon 0 - Grundy 36.2). Traced from OSM end to end, no straight-line legs. Routing: 34.8 mi on N&W-tagged ways and 1.1 mi on untagged rail at the Devon junction. The route runs from Devon station east along the N&W main line, over the Tug Fork at Looney's Curve and through the 1930 tunnel to Knox Creek, then Woodman - Argo - Kelsa - Hurley, the Raitt (Summit) tunnel, Home Creek, Weller/Thomas and up the Levisa Fork to Grundy. This is the line's own era alignment (built 1928-31 and still in place as the Norfolk Southern Buchanan Branch), so no later-alignment caveat applies. Waypoint fit: Kelsa's Nominatim hamlet point is 1.2 km off the line; all others are within 0.3 km. Grundy end is the branch vertex nearest the town node.",
    "segments": [
     {
      "start": 1948,
      "end": 1951,
      "headway_min": 1440,
      "note": "N&W mixed train Devon, W.Va. - Woodman - Bill - Argo - Kelsa - Luke - Hurley - Raitt - Home Creek - Thomas - Harman - Grundy, Va. (36.2 mi). 1948 and 1951 are the FIRST and LAST CONFIRMED years, NOT the start and end of service. 1948: Fowler marks Kopp, a station on this branch, '1948t', i.e. named in a 1948 N&W public timetable. 1951: the Official Guide card of 18 Nov 1951 (Feb 1952 issue, N&W Table 25) shows mixed trains M312 (Devon 8:40 AM - Grundy 11:25 AM) and M311 (Grundy 1:10 PM - Devon 3:15 PM), both daily except Sunday, with flag stops at Bill, Argo, Kelsa and Luke. The N&W took operation on 1 July 1931, but no source dates its first passenger train. Fowler's 1939 Guide mark for Weller may be only an index entry and is not counted. No source dates the last run. Both ends are withheld unknowns: do not extend either way without evidence. headway_min 1440 = one round trip a day (daily except Sunday), read from the 1951 card. A one-off Norfolk Southern 21st Century Steam excursion ran Grundy - Devon in 2014. It is a special, not a service span, and is not drawn.",
      "sources": [
       "Segment-level: end 1951 and the frequency/running times from the Official Guide of the Railways (Feb 1952), N&W p. 469 Table 25, card of 18 Nov 1951 (page image; OCR loses the times). Start 1948 from Fowler's Virginia list, line 72 (Kopp '1948t' = 1948 company public timetable). 1 July 1931 N&W takeover from the N&W 1931 annual report via Railway Age 2 Apr 1932 (bounds only, not a passenger date).",
       "https://archive.org/download/the-official-guide-of-the-railways-images/page/n460.jpg",
       "https://www.branchline.uk/jfpdf/virginiarrs.pdf",
       "https://archive.org/details/sim_railway-age_1932-04-02_92_14",
       "https://nwhs.org/commissary/Buchanan.NW.Branch.Lines.html"
      ]
     }
    ]
